    <div class="titleText">
  
    







  
<section id="un3">
<div class="w-li-container" data-check="blogpage" style="background-color: #fff  !important;">
   
  <div class="w-li-header" style="text-align:;font-size:">Overview</div>
      <div class="limain-wli">

          

          <div class="w-li-main-para" style="font-size:"> <p>Bajaj Life Insurance Limited, formerly known as Bajaj Allianz Life Insurance Company Limited, is one of India’s fastest-growing private life insurers. Our organisation is transitioning to being 100% owned by the Bajaj Group – a household name in India with a 100-year legacy of trust and credibility. As part of Bajaj Finserv Limited, one of the country’s most diversified and respected financial services groups, we bring innovation, a customer-first mindset, and technology-led solutions to the forefront. Today, we stand as a trusted partner to over 3.42<sup>##</sup> crore Indians in securing their future.</p>
<p>At a Glance, numbers you should know</p>
<ul class="with_dots"><li>₹1.46 Lakh Cr***  Assets Under Management</li><li>266%<sup>^^^</sup> Solvency Margin</li><li>99.33%<sup>~</sup> Claim Settlement Ratio</li><li>598 Branches</li><li>1.64 Lakh&#43; Insurance Consultants (as on September, 2026)</li><li>26,356 Bajaj Life Employees (as on September, 2026)</li></ul>
<p>We offer a diverse range of plans to support Life Goals at every stage. Our life insurance products ranging from ULIPs with Zero Allocation Charges to the SISO Investment Approach are built to drive long-term growth. Our holistic term plans address specific needs, whether it’s cover for diabetics, or the Superwoman Term Plan with enhanced critical illness benefits. Every product is thoughtfully designed to meet the Life Goals of millions of Indians.</p>
<p>Driven by innovation and inclusivity, we remain committed in enabling customers achieve their Life Goals through value-driven, innovative products that are simple to understand, affordable and designed to address long-term needs such as protection, wealth creation, retirement planning, and more. These offerings are supported by a comprehensive suite of future driven, digital-first services across customer touchpoints, ensuring seamless accessibility and convenience.</p>
<p>We have a robust distribution network of 598 branches and over 1,64,917 agents (as on September, 2026), complemented by partnerships with leading Indian banks as well as wide network of corporate agents, providing customers with convenient access to our products.</p>
<p> </p>
<p><a href="https://www.bajajfinserv.in/corporate-bajaj-finserv#">BFS: https://www.bajajfinserv.in/corporate-bajaj-finserv#</a></p>
<p>Bajaj Life Insurance Limited (formerly known as Bajaj Allianz Life Insurance Company Limited) is one of India’s leading, most trusted and dynamic private life insurance companies. It is a subsidiary of Bajaj Finserv Limited, India’s leading and most diversified financial services group.</p>
<p>Bajaj Life has emerged as one of the fastest-growing life insurers in the country, backed by the trusted legacy of the Bajaj Group. With a comprehensive life insurance portfolio, it offers tailored solutions across a wide spectrum — from ULIPs, Term Plans, and Child Plans to Group and Health Insurance — meeting the diverse Life Goals of individuals and businesses alike.</p>
<p>Driven by competitive pricing, product innovation, and customer-first thinking, Bajaj Life has earned the trust of millions and cemented its place as a preferred Life Goals enabler. </p>
</div>
      </div>
  </div>
  </section>


  
    

</div>


    
    
    <div class="leadership">

  
    
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/etc.clientlibs/balic-web/components/leadership/clientLibs.lc-d52ac6e16a7de848da91e5eb86769253-lc.min.css" type="text/css">
<script src="/etc.clientlibs/balic-web/components/leadership/clientLibs.lc-b11bd61e2001e3343ccbf1ea43f3ca15-lc.min.js"></script>







<div class="leaders-container">
  <div class="h1">Our Leaders</div>
  <div class="ltli-item">
    
      <div class="people_of_balic">
        <li onclick="showleadercard(event)" bgcolor="#F2F2F2" attr="Board of Directors">Board of Directors</li>
      </div>
    
      <div class="people_of_balic">
        <li onclick="showleadercard(event)" bgcolor="rgba(48,112,182,0.2)" attr="Leadership Team">Leadership Team</li>
      </div>
    
      <div class="people_of_balic">
        <li onclick="showleadercard(event)"></li>
      </div>
    
  </div>

  
    

    <div id="Board of Directors" class="leader-box dsp-none">
      <div class="leader-items-wrapper">
      
        <div class="bfd-box">
          <img loading="lazy" class="bfdsvg-left" src="/content/dam/balic-web/images/ppl_of_bajaj_dots.svg" alt=""/>
          <img loading="lazy" class="bfdsvg-right" src="/content/dam/balic-web/images/ppl_of_bajaj_dots.svg" alt=""/>
          <div class="h2">Sanjiv Bajaj</div>
          <span>Chairman</span>
          <div id="Board of Directors Sanjiv Bajaj" class="lederhover-con dsp-none">
            
             <div class="lederhover-box width-fit">
              <div class="lederhover_closesvg">
                <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none">
                  <path fill-rule="evenodd" clip-rule="evenodd" d="M5.00049 17.5864C4.60999 17.977 4.61005 18.6101 5.00061 19.0006C5.39117 19.3911 6.02433 19.3911 6.41482 19.0005L12.0001 13.4143L17.5858 19C17.9763 19.3905 18.6095 19.3905 19 19C19.3905 18.6095 19.3905 17.9763 19 17.5858L13.4142 12L18.9996 6.41359C19.39 6.02303 19.39 5.38987 18.9994 4.99938C18.6089 4.60888 17.9757 4.60894 17.5852 4.9995L11.9999 10.5858L6.41414 4.99998C6.02362 4.60946 5.39045 4.60946 4.99993 4.99998C4.6094 5.39051 4.6094 6.02367 4.99993 6.4142L10.5859 12.0001L5.00049 17.5864Z"/>
                </svg>
              </div>
              <div class="lederh-details">
                <div class="h1">Sanjiv Bajaj</div>
                <div class="h2">Chairman</div>
                <div class="leaders_desc"><p><b>Sanjiv Bajaj</b> is the Chairman and Managing Director of Bajaj Finserv Limited, the holding company of the financial services businesses of the Bajaj Group, one of India’s oldest and largest conglomerates, with consolidated revenue of over ₹ 1,50,530 crore (USD 15.9 billion) and consolidated profit after tax of over ₹ 8,800 crore (USD 1 billion) for FY2025-26. The combined market cap of the three listed companies - Bajaj Finserv, Bajaj Finance and Bajaj Housing Finance is ₹ 8,20,716 crore (USD 86.5 billion), as on March 31, 2026.</p>
<p>Under Sanjiv’s leadership, Bajaj Finserv Limited has emerged as one of India’s leading and most diversified financial services companies with solutions across lending, life insurance, general insurance and investments. With a consumer-first, digital approach and a culture focused on innovation, it has reshaped digital consumer financing in India.</p>
<p>Sanjiv is on the board of his group operating companies as the Chairman of Bajaj Finance Limited, Bajaj Housing Finance Limited, Bajaj General Insurance Limited, Bajaj Life Insurance Limited, Bajaj Finserv Asset Management Limited and Maharashtra Scooters Limited. He is also the Managing Director of Bajaj Holdings &amp; Investment Limited (since 2012) and serves as a non-executive director at Bajaj Auto Limited.</p>
<p>Sanjiv was the President of the Confederation of Indian Industry (CII), FY 2022-23.</p>
<p>He is a member of J.P. Morgan - Asia Pacific Council, a member of the International Advisory Council of Brookings Institute, USA, and a member of the International Advisory Board of the Global Finance &amp; Technology Network (GFTN).<b> </b>Sanjiv is co-chair for India Skills Accelerators – a Ministry of Skill Development and Entrepreneurship initiative, in partnership with the World Economic Forum. He is also a member of the Board of the Indian School of Business (ISB).</p>
<p>Sanjiv also chairs India&#64;100 Foundation, CII’s non-profit initiative that champions next generation reforms shaping India’s vision for inclusive economic growth, nurturing innovation, strengthening India’s cultural influence and ensuring sustainable progress.</p>
<p>Over the years, he has received several prestigious honours for his contribution to the financial services space, including:</p>
<p>· <b>Lifetime Achievement Award</b> by Financial Express Best Banks 2026</p>
<p>- AIMA-JRD <b>Tata Corporate Leadership Award for the Year 2023</b></p>
<p>- The Lakshmipat Singhania IIM Lucknow <b>National Leadership Award, 2023</b>, received from the <b>Hon’ble President of India Smt. Droupadi Murmu</b></p>
<p>- <b>Economic Times Business Leader of the year 2018</b></p>
<p>- <b>Financial Express Best Banker of the year 2017</b></p>
<p>- <b>Ernst &amp; Young Entrepreneur of the year in 2017</b></p>
<p>- Business <b>World’s Most Valuable CEOs </b>in India for <b>2015 </b>and <b>2016</b></p>
<p>Sanjiv has a Bachelor’s degree in Mechanical Engineering from the University of Pune, a Master’s degree in Manufacturing Systems Engineering from the University of Warwick, UK, and a Master’s degree in Business Administration from the Harvard Business School, USA. He lives in Pune, Maharashtra, with his wife, Shefali and their two children.</p>
</div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      
        <div class="bfd-box">
          <img loading="lazy" class="bfdsvg-left" src="/content/dam/balic-web/images/ppl_of_bajaj_dots.svg" alt=""/>
          <img loading="lazy" class="bfdsvg-right" src="/content/dam/balic-web/images/ppl_of_bajaj_dots.svg" alt=""/>
          <div class="h2">Niraj Bajaj	</div>
          <span>Director</span>
          <div id="Board of Directors Niraj Bajaj	" class="lederhover-con dsp-none">
            
             <div class="lederhover-box width-fit">
              <div class="lederhover_closesvg">
                <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none">
                  <path fill-rule="evenodd" clip-rule="evenodd" d="M5.00049 17.5864C4.60999 17.977 4.61005 18.6101 5.00061 19.0006C5.39117 19.3911 6.02433 19.3911 6.41482 19.0005L12.0001 13.4143L17.5858 19C17.9763 19.3905 18.6095 19.3905 19 19C19.3905 18.6095 19.3905 17.9763 19 17.5858L13.4142 12L18.9996 6.41359C19.39 6.02303 19.39 5.38987 18.9994 4.99938C18.6089 4.60888 17.9757 4.60894 17.5852 4.9995L11.9999 10.5858L6.41414 4.99998C6.02362 4.60946 5.39045 4.60946 4.99993 4.99998C4.6094 5.39051 4.6094 6.02367 4.99993 6.4142L10.5859 12.0001L5.00049 17.5864Z"/>
                </svg>
              </div>
              <div class="lederh-details">
                <div class="h1">Niraj Bajaj</div>
                <div class="h2">Director</div>
                <div class="leaders_desc"><p>He has been Chairman of Mukand Ltd. since July’ 2007 and serves as its Managing Director. He is also Chairman of Bajaj Auto Ltd. and Vice Chairman of Bajaj Holdings &amp; Investment Ltd. He is also Chairman of Jamnalal Sons Pvt Ltd and Bachhraj &amp; Company Pvt Ltd.  He is one of the Promoters of the Bajaj Group. He has an entrepreneurial career spanning more than 42 years. He was selected by World Economic Forum, as one of the “Global Leaders for Tomorrow”, in 1993. He was the President of Indian Merchants’ Chamber, Alloy Steel Producer’s Association of India and Indian Stainless Steel Development Association. A three time All India Table Tennis Champion, has represented the Country for 7 years of which 4 years as Captain. He has been recipient of several prestigious awards including the Arjuna Award, Shiv Chhatrapati Award and Maharashtra Gaurav Puraskar. He brings on the Board his vast business experience in handling various matters related to managing external challenges and provides a long-term perspective that is very critical for the business.</p>
<p>He holds Bachelor’s degree in commerce from Sydenham College of Commerce and Economics, Mumbai and a Master’s degree in Business Administration from Harvard Business School, U.S.A.</p>
</div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      
        <div class="bfd-box">
          <img loading="lazy" class="bfdsvg-left" src="/content/dam/balic-web/images/ppl_of_bajaj_dots.svg" alt=""/>
          <img loading="lazy" class="bfdsvg-right" src="/content/dam/balic-web/images/ppl_of_bajaj_dots.svg" alt=""/>
          <div class="h2">Padmaja Chunduru</div>
          <span>Independent Director</span>
          <div id="Board of Directors Padmaja Chunduru" class="lederhover-con dsp-none">
            
             <div class="lederhover-box width-fit">
              <div class="lederhover_closesvg">
                <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none">
                  <path fill-rule="evenodd" clip-rule="evenodd" d="M5.00049 17.5864C4.60999 17.977 4.61005 18.6101 5.00061 19.0006C5.39117 19.3911 6.02433 19.3911 6.41482 19.0005L12.0001 13.4143L17.5858 19C17.9763 19.3905 18.6095 19.3905 19 19C19.3905 18.6095 19.3905 17.9763 19 17.5858L13.4142 12L18.9996 6.41359C19.39 6.02303 19.39 5.38987 18.9994 4.99938C18.6089 4.60888 17.9757 4.60894 17.5852 4.9995L11.9999 10.5858L6.41414 4.99998C6.02362 4.60946 5.39045 4.60946 4.99993 4.99998C4.6094 5.39051 4.6094 6.02367 4.99993 6.4142L10.5859 12.0001L5.00049 17.5864Z"/>
                </svg>
              </div>
              <div class="lederh-details">
                <div class="h1">Padmaja Chunduru</div>
                <div class="h2">Independent Director</div>
                <div class="leaders_desc"><p>She is a seasoned business leader with over 37 years of experience in banking and capital markets in India and USA. She has led iconic institutions including National Securities Depository Ltd. and Indian Bank as the MD &amp; CEO. As MD &amp; CEO of Indian Bank, she successfully steered the merger of Allahabad Bank into Indian Bank. Significant improvement in all key business metrics and the empathetic handling of the cultural integration of two diverse banks became the subject of a case study &#34;Merger of Equals&#34; by Harvard Business School Publishing. She has been on the Boards of Life Insurance Corporation of India and National Payments Corporation of India, International Securities Services Association and Asia Pacific Central Depository Group, Institute of International Bankers and Asia Society, New York. Currently she is a member of the Insurance Advisory Committee of Insurance Regulatory and Development Authority of India and the Centre for Corporate Governance and Sustainability Advisory Council, IIM Bangalore. She has been awarded Best CEO (BFSI) for 2021 by Business Today and Best CEO 2021 for Women Leadership by Economic Times. She has been acknowledged as one of the Most Powerful Women (MPW) in Business by Fortune India and Business Today, for 2022 and 2023.</p>
<p>She holds a Post-Graduate in Commerce from Andhra University.</p>
</div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      
        <div class="bfd-box">
          <img loading="lazy" class="bfdsvg-left" src="/content/dam/balic-web/images/ppl_of_bajaj_dots.svg" alt=""/>
          <img loading="lazy" class="bfdsvg-right" src="/content/dam/balic-web/images/ppl_of_bajaj_dots.svg" alt=""/>
          <div class="h2">Apurva Diwanji</div>
          <span>Independent Director</span>
          <div id="Board of Directors Apurva Diwanji" class="lederhover-con dsp-none">
            
             <div class="lederhover-box width-fit">
              <div class="lederhover_closesvg">
                <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none">
                  <path fill-rule="evenodd" clip-rule="evenodd" d="M5.00049 17.5864C4.60999 17.977 4.61005 18.6101 5.00061 19.0006C5.39117 19.3911 6.02433 19.3911 6.41482 19.0005L12.0001 13.4143L17.5858 19C17.9763 19.3905 18.6095 19.3905 19 19C19.3905 18.6095 19.3905 17.9763 19 17.5858L13.4142 12L18.9996 6.41359C19.39 6.02303 19.39 5.38987 18.9994 4.99938C18.6089 4.60888 17.9757 4.60894 17.5852 4.9995L11.9999 10.5858L6.41414 4.99998C6.02362 4.60946 5.39045 4.60946 4.99993 4.99998C4.6094 5.39051 4.6094 6.02367 4.99993 6.4142L10.5859 12.0001L5.00049 17.5864Z"/>
                </svg>
              </div>
              <div class="lederh-details">
                <div class="h1">Apurva Diwanji</div>
                <div class="h2">Independent Director</div>
                <div class="leaders_desc"><p>He is a reputed Advocate in India and Solicitor (Supreme Court of England &amp; Wales). He is the Senior Partner of Desai &amp; Diwanji, a leading law firm. With rich experience of more than three decades India and abroad, he specialises in mergers and acquisitions, international capital markets, co-investments, private equity and joint ventures. He has led and advised on a variety of transnational and cross border transactions, sale/acquisition of existing Indian companies, and public issues. He has advised on all types of M&amp;A transactions including mergers and amalgamations, asset and business purchases and sales, securities sales and purchases, tender offers, buy-outs, joint ventures and strategic buy outs. He advises on the full spectrum of such matters including corporate governance issues, transaction structuring FDI and FEMA issues, SEBI regulations and has advised on transactions across various industry sectors. He has also been advising on corporate governance and minority protection issues and large corporate disputes.</p>
<p>He has completed M.A. in Law, Downing College, Cambridge University, UK and BA (Econ), St. Xaviers’ College, Mumbai.</p>
</div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      
        <div class="bfd-box">
          <img loading="lazy" class="bfdsvg-left" src="/content/dam/balic-web/images/ppl_of_bajaj_dots.svg" alt=""/>
          <img loading="lazy" class="bfdsvg-right" src="/content/dam/balic-web/images/ppl_of_bajaj_dots.svg" alt=""/>
          <div class="h2">Dr Srinivasa Rao Nagarjuna</div>
          <span>Director</span>
          <div id="Board of Directors Dr Srinivasa Rao Nagarjuna" class="lederhover-con dsp-none">
            
             <div class="lederhover-box width-fit">
              <div class="lederhover_closesvg">
                <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none">
                  <path fill-rule="evenodd" clip-rule="evenodd" d="M5.00049 17.5864C4.60999 17.977 4.61005 18.6101 5.00061 19.0006C5.39117 19.3911 6.02433 19.3911 6.41482 19.0005L12.0001 13.4143L17.5858 19C17.9763 19.3905 18.6095 19.3905 19 19C19.3905 18.6095 19.3905 17.9763 19 17.5858L13.4142 12L18.9996 6.41359C19.39 6.02303 19.39 5.38987 18.9994 4.99938C18.6089 4.60888 17.9757 4.60894 17.5852 4.9995L11.9999 10.5858L6.41414 4.99998C6.02362 4.60946 5.39045 4.60946 4.99993 4.99998C4.6094 5.39051 4.6094 6.02367 4.99993 6.4142L10.5859 12.0001L5.00049 17.5864Z"/>
                </svg>
              </div>
              <div class="lederh-details">
                <div class="h1">Dr. Srinivasa Rao Nagarjuna</div>
                <div class="h2">Director</div>
                <div class="leaders_desc"><p>He is currently working as Chief Economist and President at Bajaj Finserv Limited. He is a public policy specialist and economist of repute with over 29 years of experience in both Central and State Governments. Prior to this role, he had been Economic Advisor, Ministry of Finance, Govt. of India as a member of the esteemed Indian Economic Service (IES). He held key positions across both the Union and State Governments, as well as Regulatory bodies, specialising in framing, implementing, and evaluating macroeconomic frameworks, as well as financial and development policies.<b></b></p>
<p><b> </b></p>
<p>He was actively involved in the mergers of Public Sector banks and spearheaded the listing of India’s national reinsurer, GIC and the New India Assurance Ltd. Underlining his multifaceted engagements in the financial and regulatory landscape, he also held extensive board positions at some of the leading financial institutions such as Indian Bank, Vijaya Bank, Oriental Insurance Company, Agricultural Insurance Company Ltd, apart from being a member on the Insurance Advisory Committee and also on the Governing board of National Insurance Academy, Institute of Actuaries and the Board of Insurance Regulatory and Development  Authority of India.<b></b></p>
<p>His academic background includes a Postgraduate degree in Economics and a Ph.D. in Public Finance from the University of Hyderabad and a graduate degree from SRCC, Delhi University.</p>
</div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      
        <div class="bfd-box">
          <img loading="lazy" class="bfdsvg-left" src="/content/dam/balic-web/images/ppl_of_bajaj_dots.svg" alt=""/>
          <img loading="lazy" class="bfdsvg-right" src="/content/dam/balic-web/images/ppl_of_bajaj_dots.svg" alt=""/>
          <div class="h2">Sanjiv Sahai</div>
          <span>Independent Director</span>
          <div id="Board of Directors Sanjiv Sahai" class="lederhover-con dsp-none">
            
             <div class="lederhover-box width-fit">
              <div class="lederhover_closesvg">
                <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none">
                  <path fill-rule="evenodd" clip-rule="evenodd" d="M5.00049 17.5864C4.60999 17.977 4.61005 18.6101 5.00061 19.0006C5.39117 19.3911 6.02433 19.3911 6.41482 19.0005L12.0001 13.4143L17.5858 19C17.9763 19.3905 18.6095 19.3905 19 19C19.3905 18.6095 19.3905 17.9763 19 17.5858L13.4142 12L18.9996 6.41359C19.39 6.02303 19.39 5.38987 18.9994 4.99938C18.6089 4.60888 17.9757 4.60894 17.5852 4.9995L11.9999 10.5858L6.41414 4.99998C6.02362 4.60946 5.39045 4.60946 4.99993 4.99998C4.6094 5.39051 4.6094 6.02367 4.99993 6.4142L10.5859 12.0001L5.00049 17.5864Z"/>
                </svg>
              </div>
              <div class="lederh-details">
                <div class="h1">Sanjiv Sahai</div>
                <div class="h2">Independent Director</div>
                <div class="leaders_desc"><p>He is a former IAS officer and has been a part of policy making at the highest levels, both in the Government of India and state government: as Director in Prime Minister’s Office, as Additional Secretary and subsequently as Secretary in the Ministry of Power. He has worked in the infrastructure sector for over 26 years and has vast experience and first-hand knowledge of issues such as infrastructure financing, risks and contract management. He was part of the Taskforce on infrastructure set up by the then Prime Minister.  As a key member in the Prime Minister’s Office (1998-2003), he has handled, amongst others, formulation of strategies and policies for infrastructure development, the highways and telecom sectors, senior appointments in the government of India, judiciary, armed forces, banks, public sector undertakings,</p>
<p>As the Finance Secretary of Delhi Government (2015-18) he transitioned VAT to GST. Concurrently as the Chairman of Delhi Financial Corporation, he managed the risks in lending and recoveries in the SME sector and also improved the quality of assets. As the Secretary in Ministry of Power, Govt. of India (2019-21), he formulated policies to enhance the sustainability of the power sector, encouraging investment in renewables and improving grid management.</p>
<p>He has also worked in the private sector as a member of the Tata Administrative Service, and later as Advisor in Infrastructure Development Finance Company (IDFC) and as MD &amp; CEO of Delhi Integrated Multimodal Transit System Ltd.</p>
<p>He has completed a Masters in Public Policy, Princeton University, USA (Specialisation: Financial Management and Economic Policy), Master of Arts, Delhi University and Bachelor of Arts, Delhi University</p>
</div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      
        <div class="bfd-box">
          <img loading="lazy" class="bfdsvg-left" src="/content/dam/balic-web/images/ppl_of_bajaj_dots.svg" alt=""/>
          <img loading="lazy" class="bfdsvg-right" src="/content/dam/balic-web/images/ppl_of_bajaj_dots.svg" alt=""/>
          <div class="h2">S Sreenivasan</div>
          <span>Director</span>
          <div id="Board of Directors S Sreenivasan" class="lederhover-con dsp-none">
            
             <div class="lederhover-box width-fit">
              <div class="lederhover_closesvg">
                <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none">
                  <path fill-rule="evenodd" clip-rule="evenodd" d="M5.00049 17.5864C4.60999 17.977 4.61005 18.6101 5.00061 19.0006C5.39117 19.3911 6.02433 19.3911 6.41482 19.0005L12.0001 13.4143L17.5858 19C17.9763 19.3905 18.6095 19.3905 19 19C19.3905 18.6095 19.3905 17.9763 19 17.5858L13.4142 12L18.9996 6.41359C19.39 6.02303 19.39 5.38987 18.9994 4.99938C18.6089 4.60888 17.9757 4.60894 17.5852 4.9995L11.9999 10.5858L6.41414 4.99998C6.02362 4.60946 5.39045 4.60946 4.99993 4.99998C4.6094 5.39051 4.6094 6.02367 4.99993 6.4142L10.5859 12.0001L5.00049 17.5864Z"/>
                </svg>
              </div>
              <div class="lederh-details">
                <div class="h1">S Sreenivasan</div>
                <div class="h2">Director</div>
                <div class="leaders_desc"><p>He is currently President – Insurance &amp; Special Projects of Bajaj Finserv Limited, the holding company of the Company. He previously served as the Chief Financial Officer of Bajaj Finserv Limited for over a decade. He has been the Chairman of the National Committee of Chief Financial Officers (CFO) of the Confederation of Indian Industry. He was chosen CFO of the year (BFSI) by the CII in 2021 and is actively involved in standards forums and advisory committee of the Securities and Exchange Board of India (SEBI).</p>
<p>He has nearly four decades of experience as a senior finance professional in a variety of assignments in India and abroad. Prior to joining Bajaj Finserv Limited in 2011, he has held senior positions in Bajaj General Insurance Limited (previously Bajaj Allianz General Insurance Co. Ltd.) as CFO, Bahrain National Holding Company (a holding Company for general and life insurance businesses) apart from early stints in Thermax Devilbiss Limited and Bajaj Auto Limited.</p>
<p>Apart from a deep insight into various aspects of life, general and health insurance, he has significant expertise in a wide gamut of areas including business strategy, planning, corporate finance, portfolio management, risk management and various aspects of general management of companies.</p>
<p>He holds a Bachelor’s Degree of Science (Physics, Mathematics and Statistics) from the University of Kerala, a Chartered Accountant, a Cost Accountant, a Chartered Financial Analyst (CFA Institute, Virginia, USA), MBA from the Indian Institute of Management, Calcutta. He was the first rank in Kerala University in B Sc. (Physics) and featured in the All India Merit list for CA Intermediate and final examinations.</p>
</div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      
        <div class="bfd-box">
          <img loading="lazy" class="bfdsvg-left" src="/content/dam/balic-web/images/ppl_of_bajaj_dots.svg" alt=""/>
          <img loading="lazy" class="bfdsvg-right" src="/content/dam/balic-web/images/ppl_of_bajaj_dots.svg" alt=""/>
          <div class="h2">Anup Wadhawan</div>
          <span>Independent Director</span>
          <div id="Board of Directors Anup Wadhawan" class="lederhover-con dsp-none">
            
             <div class="lederhover-box width-fit">
              <div class="lederhover_closesvg">
                <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none">
                  <path fill-rule="evenodd" clip-rule="evenodd" d="M5.00049 17.5864C4.60999 17.977 4.61005 18.6101 5.00061 19.0006C5.39117 19.3911 6.02433 19.3911 6.41482 19.0005L12.0001 13.4143L17.5858 19C17.9763 19.3905 18.6095 19.3905 19 19C19.3905 18.6095 19.3905 17.9763 19 17.5858L13.4142 12L18.9996 6.41359C19.39 6.02303 19.39 5.38987 18.9994 4.99938C18.6089 4.60888 17.9757 4.60894 17.5852 4.9995L11.9999 10.5858L6.41414 4.99998C6.02362 4.60946 5.39045 4.60946 4.99993 4.99998C4.6094 5.39051 4.6094 6.02367 4.99993 6.4142L10.5859 12.0001L5.00049 17.5864Z"/>
                </svg>
              </div>
              <div class="lederh-details">
                <div class="h1">Anup Wadhawan</div>
                <div class="h2">Independent Director</div>
                <div class="leaders_desc"><p>He is a former IAS officer and experienced economic and public policy professional with over 41 years’ experience in various sectors including the civil service, regulation, academia, private sector and international development agencies. In Government he acquired experience at the National, Provincial &amp; Field / District level, including in leadership roles in framing / implementing economic / development policy. He served as the Commerce Secretary to the Government of India for 3 years. He was also Director General of Foreign Trade, Additional / Joint Secretary in Dept. of Financial Services, Joint Secretary, Capital Markets in the Dept. of Economic Affairs and Director in the Prime Minister&#39;s Office. At the provincial level he was Principal Secretary / Secretary to the Govt. of Uttarakhand in various departments ranging from Urban Development, Forests and Environment to Home. While in Govt. he also held Board positions in various public sector undertakings of Govt. of India like Government E-Marketplace, Bank of India, and the Agriculture Insurance Company of India, and in regulatory bodies like Insurance Regulatory and Development Authority of India and the Pension Fund Regulatory and Development Authority. He also served / taught in international developmental and academic institutions.</p>
<p>He has completed a Ph.D. in Economics from Duke University, USA, a Master’s degree in Economics from Delhi School of Economics and a Bachelor of Arts (Hons) degree in Economics from Delhi University.</p>
</div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      
        <div class="bfd-box">
          <img loading="lazy" class="bfdsvg-left" src="/content/dam/balic-web/images/ppl_of_bajaj_dots.svg" alt=""/>
          <img loading="lazy" class="bfdsvg-right" src="/content/dam/balic-web/images/ppl_of_bajaj_dots.svg" alt=""/>
          <div class="h2">Tarun Chugh</div>
          <span>Managing Director and Chief Executive Officer</span>
          <div id="Board of Directors Tarun Chugh" class="lederhover-con dsp-none">
            
             <div class="lederhover-box width-fit">
              <div class="lederhover_closesvg">
                <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none">
                  <path fill-rule="evenodd" clip-rule="evenodd" d="M5.00049 17.5864C4.60999 17.977 4.61005 18.6101 5.00061 19.0006C5.39117 19.3911 6.02433 19.3911 6.41482 19.0005L12.0001 13.4143L17.5858 19C17.9763 19.3905 18.6095 19.3905 19 19C19.3905 18.6095 19.3905 17.9763 19 17.5858L13.4142 12L18.9996 6.41359C19.39 6.02303 19.39 5.38987 18.9994 4.99938C18.6089 4.60888 17.9757 4.60894 17.5852 4.9995L11.9999 10.5858L6.41414 4.99998C6.02362 4.60946 5.39045 4.60946 4.99993 4.99998C4.6094 5.39051 4.6094 6.02367 4.99993 6.4142L10.5859 12.0001L5.00049 17.5864Z"/>
                </svg>
              </div>
              <div class="lederh-details">
                <div class="h1">Tarun Chugh</div>
                <div class="h2">Managing Director and Chief Executive Officer</div>
                <div class="leaders_desc"><p>Tarun has been the transformational leader behind the sustained growth of Bajaj Life, which is now one of the fastest-growing private life insurers amongst top companies in the country. The Company is ~26K team strong, operates across over 598 branches, has India’s only Agency channel that is 100% digital with has a network of around 1.64&#43; lakh Insurance Consultants (agents). The Company offers Bespoke Banca experience to India’s leading Banks and financial institutes and is proud to have India’s leading Direct channel.<b></b></p>
<p>At Bajaj Life, every aspect of the business continues to be guided by its Customer First approach. It has enabled it to redefine its products suite, enhance its distribution, elevate and simplify its services and processes. These initiatives continue to strengthen the Company’s brand promise &#34;Life Goals. DONE.&#34;, under Tarun’s leadership. A strong advocate for innovation and employee empowerment, he has introduced several unique initiatives for customer delight as well as employee development. Today, Bajaj Life Insurance leads the industry across parameters. From its comprehensive suite of life goals enabling products, tech-empowered service eco-system, digital assets to delight all stakeholders while they engage with the Company, as well as a team that thinks innovation and delivers on customer delight.</p>
<p>Tarun’s rich industry tenure of over three decades, includes leadership roles at PNB Met Life and ICICI Prudential Life Insurance. His rich experience continues to fuel his transformational approach to create sustained innovation and growth within the Company. His engagement extends to industry and academia. He serves on governing councils and advisory boards, including IIM Sambalpur. An IIT Delhi and IIM Lucknow alumnus, Tarun resides with his family in Mumbai.</p></div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      
      </div>
      <div class="leader-description"></div>
    </div>
  
    <div id="Leadership Team" class="leader-box dsp-none">
      <div class="leader-items-wrapper">
      
        <div class="leder-item" attr2="Tarun Chugh&lt;br>&lt;span>Managing Director and Chief Executive Officer&lt;/span>">
          <div class="lederitem-img">
            <img loading="lazy" src="/content/dam/balic-web/images/revamp-images/Tarun-Sir.webp" alt=""/>
